From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:13:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 48/49] Debye line hooks keep their per-step transients in
 per-thread scratch

A packed Debye group stored, beside the state W of its poles, the
pre-sum its Pre hook hands to its Post hook and the correction its Post
hook hands to its Apply hook: 24 of 12*(P+2) floats a group that were
written to and read back from the large block every timestep only to
cross two calls.

Engine_Extension gets RANGE_LOCAL and SetRangeLocal(): after every plan
the multithreaded engine tells the extensions that declare it whether
the plan calls each Pre, Post, Apply of one range (x-line block or
x-y box) back to back on one thread, and the widest range. It does for
the fused sweep in line blocks, its y-bands with an open y direction
and the box mode of the tiled sweep; not for the unfused plan, the
tiled sweep's hook stages or y-bands of a closed y direction. While
granted, the Debye blocks hold W only (moved together inside the same
allocation) and the two transients live in a scratch slice of the
calling thread, 24 floats a group of the range; a check of thread,
width and call order stops the run if the engine breaks the grant.
Per-lane arithmetic and its order are unchanged; results stay
bit-identical. Lorentz and Drude state is read again in the next
timestep and is left as it was.

OPENEMS_ADE_SCRATCH=0 keeps the stored layout; =alt (test) withdraws
and grants again before every run of timesteps.

Checked bit-identical against the commit before and against v0.37.0:
501 box configurations in three variants (1 to 4 poles, lanes 4 to 1
and a split mask, both group kinds, every driver, 1 to 6 threads,
closed cylinder), the dispersive check at 50 k and 1 M cells, five
models without Debye, the Debye check and the validation suite; seven
planted faults each caught.

Mac Studio (M5 Max), upstream bench.py with a source, dispersive case,
18 threads, MC/s before -> after: 30 M cells 2969 -> 3266, 8 M cells
2964 -> 3156, 1 M cells 3923 -> 4054. At 8 M cells and 6 threads (no
y-bands) 1920 -> 1860. Antenna case 1.00 to 1.01, the two boards 1.00
and 1.01 at 18 threads.

